  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Synapse Creature" id="c531-2ba5-638d-73d5" hidden="false">
      <description>This power is always on and does not require a psychic test ot use. Any Tyranid unit with a model within 12&quot; of the creature never have to fall back and are assumed to automatically pass any Morale checks they are required to take.


Any Pinning checks and tests to regroup are also passed automatically.
In addition, the creature is able to cause all Spore Mines with 24&quot; to detonate in the Shooting phase, instead of shooting any of its own weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Instinctive Behavior" id="dea2-e710-8473-b3ed" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the Tyranid turn any broods outside Synapse countrol range must take a Morale check for being All On Your Own. If failed consult the Tyranid Instinctive Behavior table. Additionally, roll on this table if a Tyranid creature fails a normal Morale or Pinning test while outside the Synapse control range.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fast and Deadly" id="cc35-d2b7-36a2-d9da" hidden="false">
      <description>Tyranids always roll one D6 more than normal when checking to see how far they can move through difficult ground. However, if a brood of eight or model models rolls two or more 6&apos;s on the dice it suffers one wound from the stampeded (saving throws apply as normal).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shoot the Big Ones!" id="e5fa-b52a-258b-5e3d" hidden="false">
      <description>The opposing player&apos;s line of fire is only blocked by terrain, vehicles and models in close combat while shooting at Tyranid models.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Monstrous Creatures" id="afea-f57b-bf0d-614e" hidden="false">
      <description>-Automatically passes any Morale checks and cannot be pinned


-Can allocate close combat attacks to a specific enemy in base-to-base contact and shoot at enemies not targeted by it&apos;s joined unit


-May re-roll Difficult Terrain unless joined to a unit


-Ignores enemy Armor Saves in close combat and roll S+2D6 for vehicle armor penetration


-Counts as a unit of troops for victory conditions</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Spore Mines" id="2bcd-07b5-747a-af83" hidden="false">
      <description>Spore Mines drift D6&quot; in a random direction in each Tyranid Movement phase. On a Hit symbol on the scatter dice the Tyranid player may choose the direction of movement. Unlike other models the spore can move within 1&quot; of enemy models, and if they make contact with an enemy model it detonates.

If a Spore Mine makes contact with an enemy, or an enemy unit or vehicle shoots while within 2&quot; of it the mine explodes. If the mine is reduced to 0 wounds or otherwise killed it will also explode. They may also be intentionally destroyed by synaptic control.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scything Talons" id="959a-831b-05aa-b8cf" hidden="false">
      <description>Creatures with scything talons count as having two close combat weapons in an assault and so gain +1 attack. Creatures with two sets of scything talons gain +2 Attacks. Ranged weapons that base their number of shots on the owner&apos;s Attacks do not gain additional shots.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rending Claws" id="8560-537e-b897-32f0" hidden="false">
      <description>Tyranids with rending claws inflict a wound automatically and ignore armour saves on to-hit rolls of 6. Other successful hits must roll ot wound as normal. If the creature rolls a 6 for Armour Penetration they then can roll an additional dice to determine the total Armour Penetration value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Lash Whip" id="0b27-f22b-fa4a-6d79" hidden="false">
      <description>All enemy models in base contact with this creature reduce their number of Attacks by 1, to a minimum of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Implant Attack" id="cb0b-d474-35ae-5950" hidden="false">
      <description>A model which fails is saving throw when wounded by a creature with an Implace Attack suffers 2 wounds instead of one. Implant attacks do not affect wounds inflicted by bio-plasma.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flesh Hooks" id="38cf-0395-332e-7590" hidden="false">
      <description>Creates with flesh hooks count as being equipped with frag grenades. In addition, creatures with flesh hooks count &quot;vertically impassable&quot; pieces like high walls or cliffs as difficult terrain instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bio-plasma" id="5611-7e2e-662f-0506" hidden="false">
      <description>Creatures that use bio-plasma can make a single extra close combat Attack, worked out at double the model&apos;s Initiative. Bio-plasma can also be used by models that are within 2&quot; of the enemy as well as those in base contact.
Bio-plasma attacks hit on a roll of 4+ regardless of WS. It inflicts a single hit with Strength equal to the creatures +1 (max 10). Normal armour saves allowed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Extended Carapace" id="e52d-9272-eb2a-7f76" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Brood Telepathy" id="48ef-8ce6-3e12-9b20" hidden="false">
      <description>Genestealers outside the range of Synapse creatures do not use the instinctive behavior rules, but instead must take Morale and Pinning tests like ordinary troops.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Toxic Sacs" id="eacf-b9b7-9407-8dfa" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 Strength</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fleet of Claw" id="e0d3-28a5-37fb-1bb4" hidden="false">
      <description>Instead of shooting the model can move another D6&quot; in the shooting phase, ignoring penalties for difficult terrain.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Living Artillery" id="f26e-8b6e-546a-c021" hidden="false">
      <description>For the purposed of mission objectives the model cannot capture table quarters, hold objectives, or count as surviving troups in a Meat Grinder battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fast" id="e5e5-27a4-5fa3-484b" hidden="false">
      <description>Raveners move 9&quot; on the Movement phase and can make an Assault move up to 9&quot;. When rolling for distance moved through difficult terrain add +1 to the highest roll. Roll 3D6 for fall back and pursuit distances.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Catalyst" id="3b12-1c99-e197-8b80" hidden="false">
      <description>This power may be used per turn at the beginning of the Tyranid Assault Phase and requires a Psychic test to use.
If successful, the Tyranid player can nominate a single Tyranid unit that is within 18&quot;. Models in the affected unit will strike back in close combat even if killed before their turn to attack. Remove the killed models after they have made their attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psychic Scream" id="db25-94d0-1029-694e" hidden="false">
      <description>This power is always active and does not require a Psychic test to use. Any enemy units with models within 12&quot; of a creature with this power suffer a -1 modifier to all Leadership bases testings, including Morale and Pinning tests. This modify can stack with other model&apos;s Psychic Scream abilities.
Enemy psykers within range suffer the penalty when testing use psychic powers, and ANY failed Psychic test results in a Perils of the Warp attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Horror" id="1145-b9af-3e5e-f939" hidden="false">
      <description>This power is always on and does not require a Pyschic test to use. Any enemy unit that wishes to assault a creature with this power must take a Morale check. If the check is failed the unit cannot charge the model, and cannot make any other charges that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warp Field" id="f50d-26b1-c947-b50d" hidden="false">
      <description>This power is always active and does not require a psychic test to use. Defensive barriers give this create a 2+ armour save. Note this is not an invulerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ferocious" id="b131-2f3f-d5c2-700b" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 Strength and +1 Initiative. Fericious troops must assault if there are any targets in range and must perform a sweeping advance. When a brood is subject to Ferocity the normal Deep Strike rule that models are destroyed if they land within 1&quot; of an enemy model does not apply. Instead, any enemy models that are also under, or partially under, the large template mayy be attack in close combat. This is done in the Assault phase and is conducted normally with the Tryanids counting as charging.
But, at the end of each Assault phase of the Tyranid player&apos;s turn, whether the unit has been in close combat or not, resolve a Strength 2 hit on each Ferocious brood member on the table, with no Armour save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Without Number!" id="c933-82a4-d069-b937" hidden="false">
      <description>The brood is always subject to the Sustained Attack special rule. When the brood is destroyed or if it is falling back and the Tyranid player chooses to remove it, then an identical brood re-enters play during the next Tyranid turn, arriving by mycetic spore. The replacement brood can therefore Deep Strike even if this is not allowed in the scenario being played.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Seeding Swarm" id="c532-77f0-dae5-2872" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Tyranid player gets to choose the scenario then the Tyranids will automatically be the attackers and must choose a scenario from the category of Battle.
All three missions under Battle use the Deep Strike rule, and all models in the Tyranid Seeding Swarm must arrive on the table by this method. The exception are Tyranid broods with the infiltrate rule and Lictors.
For all other scenarios, if the Deep Strike option exists it can only be used by Tyranid units with the Deep Strike rule.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
